<title>SOUTH KOREA: Strikes cost S.Korea 1.48 trln won in lost output.</title>
<headline>Strikes cost S.Korea 1.48 trln won in lost output.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea saw 1.48 trillion won in lost production as of Tuesday due to nationwide labour strikes, a trade ministry official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Lost exports from the start of industrial action on December 26 were estimated at $291 million, he said.  </p>
<p>South Korea's major industries have been crippled by strikes in protest at the passage of a new labour law, which allows employers to lay off workers, replace strikers and implement flexible work hours.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
